18. šul {d}utu |GIRI₃×X|-re-ne amar sumun₂-na#-ke₄
#tr.en: Youthful @wDN{Utu} ……, calf of the wild cow,
#lem: šul[youth]; Utu[1]DN; X; amar[calf]; sumun[wild cow]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. amar sumun₂-na-ke₄ amar dumu zid-da-ke₄
#tr.en: calf of the wild cow, calf of the righteous son,
#lem: amar[calf]; sumun[wild cow]; amar[calf]; dumu[child]; zid[right]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. {d}utu šeš lugal {d}inana-ke₄
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, royal brother of @wDN{Inana}!
#lem: Utu[1]DN; šeš[brother]; lugal[king]; Inanak[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. en-me-en de₆-de₆ sila sir₂-ra-ke₄
#tr.en: He who brings thirst to streets and paths (?),
#lem: en[lord]; de[carry]; sila[street]; esir[street]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. {d}utu kaš mu-un-ŋal₂ e₂ kurun-ka-ke₄
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, he of the tavern, provided beer, youthful @wDN{Utu},
#lem: Utu[1]DN; kaš[beer]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; e[house]; kurun[beer]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. šul {d}utu kaš mu-un-ŋal₂ e₂ kurun-ka-ke₄
#tr.en: he of the tavern, provided beer.
#lem: šul[youth]; Utu[1]DN; kaš[beer]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; e[house]; kurun[beer]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. šeš-ŋu₁₀ %e u₃-mu-un %s ni₂ gur₃-ru kur-še₃ ga-ba-e-da-u₅
#tr.en: (Inana speaks:) @q[Inana,Utu]{“My brother, awe-inspiring lord, let me ride with you to the mountains!
#lem: šeš[brother]; umun[lord]N; ni[fear]; gur[lift]; kur[mountain(s)]; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. %e u₃-mu-un %s an-na %e u₃-mu-un %s ni₂ gur₃-ru %e u₃-mu-un %s kur-še₃ ga-ba-e-da-u₅
#tr.en: Lord of heaven, awe-inspiring lord, lord, let me ride with you to the mountains;
#lem: umun[lord]N; an[sky]; umun[lord]N; ni[fear]; gur[lift]; umun[lord]N; kur[mountain(s)]; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. kur šim-ma-še₃ kur {ŋiš}erin-na-še₃ kur-še₃
#tr.en: to the mountains of herbs, to the mountains of cedars, to the mountains;
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; šim[aromatic substance]; kur[mountain(s)]; eren[cedar]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. kur {ŋiš}erin-na kur ha-šu-ur₂-ra-še₃ kur-še₃
#tr.en: to the mountains of cedars, the mountains of cypresses, to the mountains;
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; eren[cedar]; kur[mountain(s)]; hašur[tree]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. kur kug-ga kur za-gin₃-na-še₃ kur-še₃
#tr.en: to the mountains of silver, the mountains of lapis lazuli, to the mountains;
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; kug[metal]; kur[mountain(s)]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. kur gakkul₃-a mu-un-mu₂-mu₂-[še₃ kur-še₃]
#tr.en: to the mountains where the @fsux{gakkul} plants grow, to the mountains;
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; gakkul[heart (of a plant)]; mu[grow]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. id₂ hal-hal-la a-ki-ta su₃-ud-bi-[še₃ kur-še₃]
#tr.en: to the distant source of the rolling rivers, to the mountains.”}
#lem: id[river]; hal[roll (around)]; akita[source]; sud[distant]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. šeš-ŋu₁₀ ŋen-a ga-[...]
#tr.en: @q{“My brother, come, let me …….
#lem: šeš[brother]; ŋen[go]; X
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. šeš-ŋu₁₀ ab-šag₄-ga igi-ŋu₁₀ NE [...]
#tr.en: My brother, the midst of the sea …… my eyes.
#lem: šeš[brother]; abšag[center of the sea]; igi[eye]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. šeš-ŋu₁₀ munus-e-ne mu-[...]
#tr.en: My brother, women …….
#lem: šeš[brother]; munus[woman]; X
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. {d}utu munus-e-ne mu-[...]
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, women …….”}
#lem: Utu[1]DN; munus[woman]; X
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. %e aŋ₂ %s munus-e-ne %e mu %s mu-X nu-zu-ŋen
#tr.en: @q{“I am unfamiliar with womanly matters, with …….
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; munus[woman]; meš[penis]N; X; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. %e aŋ₂ %s munus-e-ne %e mu %s dug₄ nu-zu-ŋen
#tr.en: I am unfamiliar with womanly matters, with sexual intercourse!
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; munus[woman]; meš[penis]N; dug[speak]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. %e aŋ₂ %s munus-e-ne še su-ub nu-zu-ŋen
#tr.en: I am unfamiliar with womanly matters, with kissing!
#lem: aŋ[thing]N; munus[woman]; še[cvne]; sub[rub]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. %e mu %s dug₄ nu-zu-ŋen še su-ub nu-zu-ŋen
#tr.en: I am unfamiliar with sexual intercourse, I am unfamiliar with kissing!”}
#lem: meš[penis]N; dug[speak]; zu[know]; še[cvne]; sub[rub]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. kur-ra a-na %e mu-un-ma-al %s a-na ga-gu₇-un-de₃-en
#tr.en: @q{“Whatever exists in the mountains, let us eat that.
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; ana[what?]; mal[be]V/i; ana[what?]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. hur-saŋ-ŋa₂ a-na %e mu-un-ma-al %s a-na ga-gu₇-un-de₃-en
#tr.en: Whatever exists in the hills, let us eat that.
#lem: hursaŋ[mountain]; ana[what?]; mal[be]V/i; ana[what?]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. kur šim-ma-še₃ kur {ŋiš}erin-na-še₃
#tr.en: In the mountains of herbs, in the mountains of cedars,
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; šim[aromatic substance]; kur[mountain(s)]; eren[cedar]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. kur {ŋiš}erin-na kur ha-šu-ur₂-ra-še₃
#tr.en: in the mountains of cedars, the mountains of cypresses,
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; eren[cedar]; kur[mountain(s)]; hašur[tree]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. kur-ra a-na %e mu-un-ma-al %s a-na ga-gu₇-un-de₃-en
#tr.en: whatever exists in the mountains, let us eat that.”}
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; ana[what?]; mal[be]V/i; ana[what?]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. šim mu-un-gu₇-a-ta {ŋiš}erin mu-un-gu₇-a-ta
#tr.en: @q{“After the herbs have been eaten, after the cedars have been eaten,
#lem: šim[aromatic substance]; gu[eat]; eren[cedar]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. šu-ŋu₁₀ šu u₃-bi₂-du₃ e₂-ŋu₁₀-še₃ gi₄-mu
#tr.en: put your hand in my hand and then escort me to my house.
#lem: šu[hand]; šu[hand]; du[build]; e[house]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. e₂-ŋu₁₀-še₃ gi₄-mu e₂-ŋu₁₀ zabalam{ki}-a-ra
#tr.en: Escort me to my house, to my house in @wSN{Zabalam}.
#lem: e[house]; gi[turn]; e[house]; Zabalam[1]SN
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. ama-ŋu₁₀-še₃ gi₄-mu ama-ŋu₁₀  %e  ga-ša-an-gal-ra  %s 
#tr.en: Escort me to my mother, to my mother @wDN{Ningal}.
#lem: ama[mother]; gi[turn]; ama[mother]; Gašangal[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. ušbar-ŋu₁₀-še₃ gi₄-mu  %e  ga-ša-an-sumun₂-na-ra  %s 
#tr.en: Escort me to my mother-in-law, to @wDN{Ninsumun}.
#lem: ušbar[father-in-law]; gi[turn]; Gašansumun[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. e-rib-bi₂-ŋu₁₀ gi₄-mu  %e  {d}mu-tin-an-na-ra  %s 
#tr.en: Escort me to my sister-in-law, to @wDN{Ŋeštin-ana}.”}
#lem: erib[husband's sister]; gi[turn]; Mutinana[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. šu dili ed₂-da-ke₄ e₂ lu₂ ed₂-da-ke₄
#tr.en: For those who venture forth single-handed, who venture forth from a man's house,
#lem: šu[hand]; dili[single]; e[leave]; e[house]; lu[person]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. e₂ lu₂ ed₂-da-ke₄ šu dili ed₂-da-ke₄
#tr.en: for those who venture forth from a man's house,
#lem: e[house]; lu[person]; e[leave]; šu[hand]; dili[single]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=51

52. {d}utu ama-bi-me-en {d}utu a-a-bi-me-en
#tr.en: who venture forth single-handed, @wDN{Utu}: you are their mother,
#lem: Utu[1]DN; ama[mother]; Utu[1]DN; aya[father]
#etcsl: line-id=52

53. {d}utu nu-siki-ke₄ {d}utu nu-mu-su-e
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, you are their father. @wDN{Utu}, as for the orphans,
#lem: Utu[1]DN; nusiki[orphan]; Utu[1]DN; numunkuš[widow]
#etcsl: line-id=53

54. {d}utu nu-siki-ke₄ a-a-ni-gin₇ igi-bi ma-ra-pad₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, as for the widows, @wDN{Utu}: the orphans look to you as their father,
#lem: Utu[1]DN; nusiki[orphan]; aya[father]; igi[eye]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=54

55. {d}utu nu-mu-su-e ama-bi-gin₇ šu gi₄-gi₄-bi-me-en
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu}, you succour the widows as their mother.
#lem: Utu[1]DN; numunkuš[widow]; ama[mother]; šu[hand]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=55

56. a-lu za-da a-lu |DU.DU|
#tr.en: With you …….
#lem: X; zaʾe[you]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=56

